WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.077 --> 00:00:06.308
The North Wind and the Sun were high in the sky.

2
00:00:06.309 --> 00:00:10.870
As usual, the North Wind was bragging to the Sun.

3
00:00:10.871 --> 00:00:15.394
"Watch me blow away these clouds," he said.

4
00:00:15.395 --> 00:00:20.401
"I'm really strong—much stronger than you."

5
00:00:20.402 --> 00:00:25.240
He blew hard and all the clouds scattered.

6
00:00:25.241 --> 00:00:31.121
"See?" the North Wind said with a grin.

7
00:00:31.122 --> 00:00:34.984
"I'm the strongest one in the sky!"

8
00:00:34.985 --> 00:00:41.349
The Sun smiled. "I'm strong too," she said.

9
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.490
"Ha-ha!" The North Wind laughed loudly.

10
00:00:45.491 --> 00:00:52.079
"You? Strong? You're always gentle, not strong!"

11
00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.755
Just then the Sun spotted a man walking along the road.

12
00:00:56.756 --> 00:01:00.210
The man was wearing a warm coat.

13
00:01:00.211 --> 00:01:03.928
"Let's have a contest," the Sun said.

14
00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:09.311
"The one who makes that man remove his coat is the strongest."

15
00:01:09.312 --> 00:01:15.660
"Sure," the North Wind said, laughing again.

16
00:01:15.661 --> 00:01:18.391
"That will be easy for me.

17
00:01:18.392 --> 00:01:27.067
I'll just blow that coat right off him. Watch this!"

18
00:01:27.068 --> 00:01:30.362
The North Wind blew hard.

19
00:01:30.363 --> 00:01:35.376
On the road below, dust and leaves flew everywhere.

20
00:01:35.377 --> 00:01:42.879
"Oh!" The man shivered. "What a chilly wind!"

21
00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:49.580
"That's odd." The North Wind frowned as the man buttoned up his coat.

22
00:01:49.581 --> 00:01:54.509
"The coat is still on him. I'll try again."

23
00:01:54.510 --> 00:02:01.937
The North Wind blew again, this time even harder.

24
00:02:01.938 --> 00:02:06.767
But once more, the coat stayed on the man.

25
00:02:06.768 --> 00:02:15.325
"Phew!" By now the North Wind was out of breath and very tired.

26
00:02:15.326 --> 00:02:25.391
"Oh well," the Sun said gently. "I guess it's my turn."

27
00:02:25.392 --> 00:02:28.991
She moved closer to the man.

28
00:02:28.992 --> 00:02:33.301
"What strange weather," the man said, unbuttoning his coat.

29
00:02:33.302 --> 00:02:35.651
"Now it's lovely out!"

30
00:02:35.652 --> 00:02:41.224
The Sun beamed even more brightly.

31
00:02:41.225 --> 00:02:47.078
"Ahh. It's so warm," the man said. "It feels wonderful."

32
00:02:47.079 --> 00:02:55.193
"Oh no!" the North Wind cried as the man removed his coat.

33
00:02:55.194 --> 00:03:01.872
The Sun smiled. "I guess I won the contest."

34
00:03:01.873 --> 00:03:06.895
"Hmpf!" The North Wind said, taking off.

35
00:03:06.896 --> 00:03:10.608
Below, the man was resting peacefully under a tree.

36
00:03:10.609 --> 00:03:19.746
The Sun kept him warm as he slept.

37
00:03:19.747 --> 00:03:23.009
"Poor North Wind," the Sun thought.

38
00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:26.397
"Someday he'll realize something.

39
00:03:26.398 --> 00:03:35.892
It's often better to be gentle than to blow with great strength."

